  'wiz.b2helpHtml': `<h3>Backblaze B2 setup guide</h3>
<div style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.7">
<p><b>1. Create an Application Key</b><br>
B2 console → Application Keys → Add a New Application Key<br>
Name it anything, select your bucket, choose Read and Write.<br>
After creating, copy <b>keyID</b> (→ Access Key) and <b>applicationKey</b> (→ Secret Key).<br>
<span style="color:#ef4444">Note: the applicationKey is shown only once — it disappears when you close the dialog!</span></p>
<p><b>2. Copy the Endpoint</b><br>
In the B2 console, open your bucket and copy the <b>Endpoint</b> string (e.g. s3.us-west-004.backblazeb2.com), then paste it into the S3 Endpoint field above.</p>
<p><b>3. Configure CORS (uploads will fail without it)</b><br>
The B2 web console's CORS settings don't fully cover the S3 API — use the CLI:<br>
<code style="background:#f1f5f9;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px">pip install b2</code><br>
<code style="background:#f1f5f9;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px">b2 account authorize</code> (enter the keyID and applicationKey)<br>
Then run:<br>
<code style="background:#f1f5f9;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px;display:block;margin:6px 0;white-space:pre-wrap">b2 bucket update YOUR-BUCKET-NAME allPrivate --cors-rules '[{"corsRuleName":"objdock","allowedOrigins":["https://your-objdock-domain"],"allowedOperations":["s3_get","s3_put","s3_head","s3_post","s3_delete"],"allowedHeaders":["*"],"maxAgeSeconds":3600}]'</code>
Replace <b>YOUR-BUCKET-NAME</b> and <b>your-objdock-domain</b> with your real values. Wait a few minutes after running for it to take effect.</p>
<p><b>4. Come back here and click "Test connection"</b> — add the account once it passes.</p>
</div>`,
